{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779464834,"nonce":"LBk+UlpESpckrFobKXozpk3b9cs=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDHPhBQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/156","origin":"github"},"title":"Investigate 0.59 m SBG vs CUAV ellipsoidal-Z disagreement (RTK-int, same NTRIP)","message":"## Summary\n\nThe SBG Ellipse-D and CUAV C-RTK 2HP report ellipsoidal Z values that differ by **0.59 m ± 18 mm**, stable over 2 hours with both receivers in RTK integer-fixed mode sharing the same NTRIP RTCM stream. The disagreement is at the GPS receiver level — both lever-arms and EKF chains check out correctly to base_link.\n\nOut of #150 topic 1 / #138 closure analysis (`~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-21/01_138_closure.md`).\n\n## Evidence (2026-05-21 deployment, 137 stationary 30 s buckets, in-water window 12:34:39 → 14:33:42 EDT)\n\n| Comparison | Mean | Stdev | Interpretation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `sbg_ekf − mav_global` | **−0.594 m** | 18 mm | Both deported to base_link, SBG reads lower |\n| `sbg_gps − mav_raw` | **−0.557 m** | 20 mm | Antenna-level disagreement; chain isn't introducing the gap |\n| `mav_raw − mav_global` | +0.888 m | 7 mm | Matches `GPS_POS1_Z = 0.890` — mavros /global at base_link ✓ |\n| `sbg_gps − sbg_ekf` | +0.925 m | 2 mm | Matches antenna-above-base_link distance — SBG ekf_nav deported correctly ✓ |\n\nBoth sides RTK integer-fixed throughout (SBG `solution_mode=4`, `status_type=7`; mavros `status=1`). No drift, no transient. Highly systematic.\n\n## What's ruled out\n\n- **Lever-arm error**: both sides verified internally consistent at the parameter level. FCU has `GPS_POS1 = (0.835, 0, -0.890) NED` + `INS_POS1 = (-0.99, 0, -0.05) NED` (mavros /global at base_link confirmed). SBG flash has IMU→CoR = `(0.58, 0, 0.03) FRD` (matches install-log measurement of SBG IMU at `(-0.577, 0, +0.029)` from base_link).\n- **Physical antenna height difference**: Trimble and CUAV pucks share the center rail (per operator + install log); phase-center delta ≤ 5 cm.\n- **Different base station**: same NTRIP RTCM stream fed to both via gabby's `rtcm_relay_node`.\n- **FCU-side altitude bias**: scanned the 2026-05-21 param dump (`bizzyboat_project11/config/fcu/2026-05-21_pre_EK3_SRC1_POSZ_change.parm`) for `BARO_ALT_OFFSET`, `GPS_DELAY_MS`, alt-related EK3 settings — nothing carries a meaningful constant bias.\n- **Different RTK quality**: both sides RTK integer fix across the entire 137-bucket sample.\n\n## Open candidate causes\n\nIn rough decreasing-likelihood order:\n\n1. **C-RTK 2HP module-internal config** (Septentrio Mosaic-H firmware-level): antenna-model setting, ARP-vs-phase-center reporting convention, internal calibration. Invisible to ArduPilot — needs direct access to the C-RTK module via its native tool (Septentrio RxTools / web interface).\n2. **SBG internal antenna phase-center model**: `Aiding → GNSS 1` panel in sbgCenter doesn't expose an antenna-model selector for Ellipse-D. The `Advanced` tab may have lower-level RTK / antenna corrections worth photographing.\n3. **Trimble vs CUAV puck phase-center offset (PCO) above mount base**: install log (`bizzyboat_project11/docs/hydro_payload_install_log.md:514`) lists this as unresolved. Typical antenna PCOs are 5–15 cm; if SBG and CUAV apply (or don't apply) different PCO models, you can see decimeter-level differences.\n4. **NTRIP base RTCM message-type parsing**: MACORS broadcasts a mix of message types (1005/1006/MSM4/MSM7/etc.). If SBG (NovAtel OEM7-class) and u-blox/Septentrio extract the base reference position from different messages with sub-meter inconsistency, the rovers would disagree.\n\n## Investigation to do\n\n- [ ] Read C-RTK 2HP firmware version + internal antenna config (via Septentrio web UI on the module's network interface; or USB to the module bypassing the FCU CAN bus).\n- [ ] Photograph sbgCenter `Advanced` tab on mercat — verify no antenna-model setting is buried there. Also `Aiding → Magnetometer` for completeness.\n- [ ] Identify exact Trimble model from the puck markings (currently only \"GNSS/MSK\" visible per install log). Look up NGS antenna calibration file → published PCO above mount base.\n- [ ] Identify CUAV C-RTK 2HP's antenna spec — Trimble or other? PCO above mount base?\n- [ ] Capture the MACORS RTCM stream content (`ros2 topic echo /bizzy/mavros/gps_rtk/send_rtcm` + RTCM parser) and check for inconsistencies between message types.\n- [ ] Optional bench-side test: place both receivers on a single benchmark with known surveyed coords; see which one is closer to ground truth.\n\n## Priority\n\n**Low-to-medium.** Doesn't block #138 closure or the June 4 class schedule. Mavros /global is the canonical nav source (already in the chart-datum chain post-§12 fix); the SBG is the payload-side INS for attitude + ship-motion. The 0.59 m disagreement just means we can't cross-check the two sources at sub-meter precision until this is understood. For survey-grade vertical chart datum work the SBG's value isn't being used, so this is more \"interesting open question\" than \"blocker.\"\n\n## Source data\n\n- Bag DB: `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-21_deployment.db`\n- Analysis writeup: `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-21/01_138_closure.md`\n- SQL used: `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-21/03_position_residuals.sql`\n- SBG flash photos: `~/sbg/2026-05-22_config/PXL_20260522_*.jpg`\n- Install log: `bizzyboat_project11/docs/hydro_payload_install_log.md:469-583`\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}